| `npm start` | Runs the release builds (by default turns into `app-all`); the edge serves the app and the API on http://localhost:{{ ports.EDGE_PORT }}. `node scripts/start.ts` keeps npm out of memory; `-- --check` prints the plan |
| `npm test` | Vitest (web and scripts) + `cargo test --workspace` |
| `npm run check` | The quality gate: ESLint + clippy, Prettier + rustfmt, vue-tsc, all tests, `npm run walls`, `npm run security` |
| `npm run walls` | `walls check` (see Quality walls); without walls it fails, in CI too (install: `npm link` in `~/Documents/walls`); only `WALLS_OPTIONAL=1` skips it with a notice, never set it to get a green check |
| `npm run security` | `secbase check` (`secbase.json`); without secbase it fails, in CI too (install: `npm link` in `~/Documents/secbase`); only `SECBASE_OPTIONAL=1` skips it with a notice, never set it to get a green check |
